WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.174
Daniel Robitaille was born on January 17, 1865, at 06:00 p.m.

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:06.234
At the Esplanade Plantation in New Orleans.

00:00:06.282 --> 00:00:08.174
He was the son of two slaves,

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:09.306
Thea B. And Wendale Robitaille.

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:11.802
But slavery was abolished just two weeks after his birth.

00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:15.194
After the American Civil War, his father, Wendale, made a considerable

00:00:15.242 --> 00:00:17.834
fortune after designing a device used to mass produce shoes.

00:00:17.882 --> 00:00:20.858
So Daniel was sent to all of the best schools and grew up in what was known

00:00:20.874 --> 00:00:22.010
as polite society.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.334
He developed a prodigious talent as an artist, and in his adulthood,

00:00:25.372 --> 00:00:28.246
many other wealthy people hired him to create portraits for them, which were

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:31.090
meant to document their wealth and be a sign of their position in society.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.794
One of these commissions came from a wealthy landowner named Hayward Sullivan,

00:00:33.842 --> 00:00:36.706
who hired Daniel to capture his daughter's virginal beauty, as he puts it. 

00:00:36.738 --> 00:00:40.406
Her name was Caroline Sullivan, and the only problem with

00:00:40.428 --> 00:00:43.978
this job is that her beauty did not stay virginal for very long.

00:00:44.064 --> 00:00:44.922
They fell in love.

00:00:44.976 --> 00:00:48.666
And in 1890, Caroline became pregnant, which was a big problem for her father,

00:00:48.688 --> 00:00:51.222
who was still transfixed by the legacy of slavery.

00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:54.842
After slavery ended, there was still a period of racial segregation,

00:00:54.896 --> 00:00:57.758
so Mr. Sullivan believed it was wrong for his white daughter to have a relationship

00:00:57.844 --> 00:00:58.798
with a black man.

00:00:58.884 --> 00:01:00.670
This was a hot button issue at the time.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.966
It was the same year that Robitaille’s home state of Louisiana passed the

00:01:03.988 --> 00:01:07.406
Separate Car Act, which required separate but equal train cars for

00:01:07.428 --> 00:01:08.094
black and white passengers.

00:01:08.142 --> 00:01:10.926
And this was just four years before the specific issue of interracial marriage

00:01:10.958 --> 00:01:13.586
would be addressed, when it would be outright prohibited in the state.

00:01:13.608 --> 00:01:16.926
But because there was no legal recourse at the time,

00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:19.744
Caroline's father hired some men to hunt Robitaille down and told them to get

00:01:19.744 --> 00:01:20.930
creative with the punishment.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.798
They finally tracked him down in an area in Chicago, Illinois,

00:01:23.804 --> 00:01:25.558
that would eventually become known as Cabrini-Green.

00:01:25.644 --> 00:01:28.614
I'm not sure why Daniel and Caroline were living there when both are from New Orleans,

00:01:28.652 --> 00:01:31.766
but it stands to reason that Caroline's father was such a

00:01:31.788 --> 00:01:34.186
wealthy landowner that he had land in multiple states.

00:01:34.288 --> 00:01:37.386
Whatever the reason may be, Daniel Robitaille was caught by the men, and they

00:01:37.408 --> 00:01:40.726
proceeded to saw off his right hand and smear his body with honey stolen

00:01:40.758 --> 00:01:41.782
from a local apiary.

00:01:41.846 --> 00:01:45.278
People in town had gathered around to watch the torture, and one kid takes a taste from

00:01:45.284 --> 00:01:49.051
the honeycomb with his finger, resulting in the coining of Robitaille's iconic nickname

00:01:49.051 --> 00:01:50.778
-[Kid] Candyman.

00:01:50.874 --> 00:01:53.918
And the whole crowd just starts chanting Candyman over and over.

00:01:54.004 --> 00:01:57.730
This is also the origin of one of Candyman's often repeated catchphrases,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.000
–[Woman] Sweets to the sweet!

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.094
The line actually comes from William Shakespeare's Hamlet at the funeral of Hamlet's love interest, Ophelia.

00:02:04.142 --> 00:02:07.026
Ophelia's mother is scattering flowers on her daughter's grave when she says

00:02:07.048 --> 00:02:07.548
the line.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.678
So this woman, saying it during the lynching of Candyman, is doing so in a

00:02:10.684 --> 00:02:11.398
mocking way.

00:02:11.484 --> 00:02:14.566
And that's when the huge swarm of bees located their stolen honeycomb and

00:02:14.588 --> 00:02:16.754
furiously attacked the man covered in their honey.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:20.502
Robitaille was stung to death by the bees, but it's said that Caroline's pain

00:02:20.556 --> 00:02:21.990
was even greater than his own.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.142
He promises that his captors will all be damned, as her father

00:02:25.206 --> 00:02:28.454
contemptuously holds her mirror up to his face to show him the monstrosities

00:02:28.502 --> 00:02:31.194
that he had become, claiming Caroline wouldn't even look at him now.

00:02:31.232 --> 00:02:35.454
Daniel Robitaille's last words are Candyman, as he passes away while

00:02:35.492 --> 00:02:36.522
staring into the mirror.

00:02:36.586 --> 00:02:39.886
But something happened that day, and when Caroline retrieves the mirror,

00:02:39.908 --> 00:02:41.822
She sees his soul captured inside of it.

00:02:41.876 --> 00:02:44.986
Witnesses said the lynching was so agonizing that his soul was trapped

00:02:45.018 --> 00:02:45.814
inside the mirror.

00:02:45.882 --> 00:02:49.038
-[Miguel] This man couldn't lash out in life, but in death.

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:53.346
-[Miguel] That hate, that evil, was strong enough to bring him back to reclaim what

00:02:53.368 --> 00:02:54.130
-[Miguel] was taken away.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.966
Sullivan's men then burned his body on a giant pyre and scattered his ashes

00:02:57.998 --> 00:02:58.738
around the area.

00:02:58.824 --> 00:03:01.862
Caroline still honored his memory at a mausoleum in their home state,

00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:04.710
inscribing the words, my beloved, may you suffer no more.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.330
But this turned out to be anything but the case.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:13.370
-[Purcell] His resurrection began as rumor and grew into myth.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.398
-[Purcell] Say his name five times in the mirror and he would appear.

00:03:17.494 --> 00:03:21.462
-[Purcell] The myth has traveled from place to place, taking root in the most desperate areas.

00:03:21.526 --> 00:03:25.566
His last name actually references the virally spreading stories and

00:03:25.588 --> 00:03:26.602
rumors about his legend.

00:03:26.666 --> 00:03:30.618
Robitaille is a French word meaning bright and famous, to learn how Candyman's

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.554
tale inspired a slew of similar legends.

00:03:32.602 --> 00:03:36.034
The true story of Candyman from our world, and the often overlooked true

00:03:36.072 --> 00:03:37.070
meaning of Candyman.

